{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event type names the purpose it is collected for, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", which is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless the type says otherwise. Give the tracker a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":", which the app updates as the user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decides, and an event reaches a destination only once its category is granted:"}]},{"code":["struct AdClicked: Event {","    static let consentCategory = ConsentCategory.advertising","    var campaign: String","}","","let consent = Consent([.analytics: .granted])","let tracker = Tracker(consent: consent)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: ConsoleDestination(),","    ConsoleDestination().accepting(.advertising)",")","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))          \/\/ delivered: analytics is granted","tracker.track(AdClicked(campaign: \"spring\"))  \/\/ held: advertising is undecided","consent.grant(.advertising)                   \/\/ delivers the held AdClicked"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A tracker given no consent delivers every event.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Undecided, granted and denied","anchor":"Undecided-granted-and-denied"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A category is undecided until the app grants or denies it. While it is undecided, its events are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held in memory, not written to a store, up to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"heldRecordLimit"},{"text":" records (1,000 by default) across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every category, the oldest dropped first when the hold is full. Granting delivers them in the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were tracked, before anything tracked after the grant. Denying drops them. Events tracked while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their category is denied are never collected.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grant"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deny"},{"text":" return at once: they record the decision, and the tracker’s worker releases or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops what it held. Every drop of a record that was held or kept is reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent.dropReports"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentDropReport"},{"text":" as it happens, so none is lost silently. Held","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records are lost if the app ends first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records that a store recovered from an earlier run are gated again as the tracker starts. They are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held outside the bound, since the store still keeps them, and the store forgets each one that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"denied."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Destinations","anchor":"Destinations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A destination receives every category the consent lets through, unless ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"text":" narrows it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the categories it serves, as the second destination above takes only advertising.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Consent Gating","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"title":"Defining Events","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","type":"topic","title":"Persisting Records","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"title":"Automatic Tracking","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"title":"Sessions and Standard Context","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","abstract":[{"text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}],"title":"Sampling Events","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","role":"article"}}}